Metadata block
A script must start with a metadata block:

// ==UserScript==
// @name Script name
// @match https://example.com/*
// ==/UserScript==

Common fields
@name: Script name.
@namespace: Combined with @name it forms the unique ID.
@match/@exclude-match: Define where the script runs and where it does not.
@include/@exclude: Legacy way of defining scopes.
@version: Script version.
@description: Script description.
@author: Script author.
@run-at: Injection time. document-start injects before the page DOM loads, document-end after DOM is ready, document-idle when the page is idle.
@updateURL/@downloadURL: Update source of the script (recorded automatically for scripts downloaded from a URL).

Match examples
// @match https://www.google.com/*
// @match *://*/*
// @exclude-match https://www.google.com/not_me

Notes
Scripts are injected automatically on matching pages. Use the switches in the list to enable or disable individual scripts. Scripts downloaded from a URL can be batch updated with the refresh button.
